Z||000000||Dan87GT||12-31-1999||08:29 AM||||   I have a question about the PCV system(system vented to the air cleaner)recall on the V6.<BR>   The two tubes that were left on the firewall after the PCV recall on my GT are both disconnected,the large tube is plugged at one end and the other smaller tube is also diconnected from the air cleaner duct to the vacuum regulator(both are plugged with screws).<BR>  My question is, is the smaller tube supposed to be dissonnected?? I thought that only the large tube was to be plugged during the recall.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Linx||01-01-2000||08:28 PM||||The small one...it's supposed to go to the EGR solenoid.  The <I>filter</I> end of the solenoid.  Have a look and see if the EGR solenoid is missing a vac' line.<P>the other end is supposed to be connected to a small tube at the base of the air filter can, via a small segment of flexible hose.<p>[This message has been edited by Linx (edited 01-01-2000).]||||reg||1
